  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "We'd love to see an improved interaction of avis in the following way: it should be possible that avis can hold each other's hands which will lead to enable one avi to guide (drag) another while walking through a world. If you think the risk for feeling nausea is too high, you could at least have both avis walk at the same speed which is the min speed of both avis, so both players can add their control to the joint movement. Currently, it is really cumbersome to coordinate speed by two individuals as you need to stop and look back. Also turning your head while walking changes direction.",
